{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe current tests inspect replacement mechanics or final JSON rather than the write window (`test_applier_mapping.py:235-282`, `test_applier_provenance.py:155-185`), permit last-writer record loss (`test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py:41-120`), and source-grep impossible-link durability (`test_impossible_links_cicada.py:467-493`). Live sidecars replace full snapshots in `peer_confirmations.py:192-217` and `impossible_links.py:376-401`. The repository already has sibling-file locked read-modify-write prior art in `_store/hlc.py::_hlc_lock` and `_commands/recent_creates.py::_journal_lock`, plus durable same-directory publication in `_store/fsutil.py::atomic_write`.\n\n## Approach\n\nGeneralize the established sibling-lock pattern in `rebar._store.fsutil` as a narrow reusable exclusive-path-lock context manager. Migrate HLC and recent-create callers to it so the project has one standard lock implementation. A lock lives at a stable sibling `.lock` path, never on the replaceable JSON inode, and remains an untracked local control artifact for the lifetime of its sidecar workspace; commit-back must not stage it. The context spans re-read, mutation, `fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True)`, and unlock.\n\nAdd `sidecar_transactions.py` only for the reconciler-specific part that existing prior art does not provide: applying a domain mutation or record delta while the shared `fsutil` lock is held. It delegates all locking and atomic publication to the generalized `fsutil` seams. Mapping/provenance mutations load the current valid mapping under that lock, apply their key-level mutation, then publish it.\n\nFor peer-confirmation and impossible-link stores, take an independent deep copy of the records loaded at construction as the immutable baseline. At save, calculate upserts and deletions against that copy; while holding the shared lock, reload the latest valid record set and apply the delta. Different keys survive. The concrete same-key rule is last shared-lock holder wins, including a deletion, so the test can assert the later lock acquisition order.\n\nIf loading valid JSON, acquiring the lock, or publishing fails, preserve the target bytes, log a path-specific warning, skip persistence for that pass, and continue the reconciliation pass fail-open. This includes malformed/non-object JSON. Readers retain old-or-new complete-document visibility through `fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True)`. Fresh-reader tests prove the existing commit-back path publishes valid state.\n\n## Scope\n\n- generalized sibling locking and durable publication reuse in `src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py`\n- HLC and recent-create adoption of that single lock seam\n- reconciler-specific `sidecar_transactions.py` delta application; mapping, peer-confirmation, and impossible-link callers\n- focused concurrency, mapping, provenance, malformed-state, and durability tests\n\n## Testing\n\nCharacterize HLC and recent-create lock migration against the prior behavior. Use barrier-controlled independent writers, same-key writers, a delete-versus-write pair, and an in-window reader for sidecars. Verify a deep baseline detects both in-place upserts and deletes, verify every lock/load/publish failure warns without overwriting, verify `.lock` files are not commit-back inputs, and prove durability through a fresh reader.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `fsutil` exposes the one sibling-path exclusive-lock primitive used by HLC, recent-create, and reconciler sidecar transactions; each caller holds it over its complete read-modify-write window.\n- [ ] The stable `.lock` file is never staged or published by commit-back and is intentionally retained for reuse while its sidecar workspace exists.\n- [ ] Reconciler sidecar publication delegates to `fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True)` rather than reimplementing temp-file replacement.\n- [ ] Mapping/provenance updates load the latest valid mapping under the shared lock before applying their key-level mutation.\n- [ ] Peer-confirmation and impossible-link stores calculate their upserts and deletions from an independent deep copy of the load-time records.\n- [ ] Concurrent distinct-key updates retain both records; a same-key test proves the later shared-lock holder wins.\n- [ ] A delete-versus-write test proves a deliberate impossible-link deletion is propagated and a later shared-lock holder determines the same-key outcome.\n- [ ] An in-window reader sees only complete pre- or post-transaction JSON.\n- [ ] A malformed target, lock failure, or atomic-write failure logs the sidecar path, preserves its bytes, and allows the reconciliation pass to continue.\n- [ ] A fresh reader proves committed mapping and impossible-link state survives publication."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788375969711552001,"uuid":"bb1ef976-e50b-4b5b-8f96-ece881ce5b5c"}